## Lessons Learned

### Defaults Matter

The default should be "works well for most people most of the time." That's `nproc - 1`:
- Fast enough (no one complains about speed)
- Responsive enough (one core keeps system alive)
- Portable (works on 4-core and 64-core machines)

Edge cases (want slower, want faster) can override.

### Environment Variables > Command Line Args

Could have done `azerothcore install --jobs=8`, but environment variable is simpler:
```bash
MAKE_JOBS=8 source scripts/azerothcore && azerothcore install
```

Why better:
- One variable for entire session
- Multiple commands (install, update) use same value
- Doesn't clutter command interface

### The One-Core Buffer

Leaving one core free prevents:
- System total freeze
- SSH disconnects (server unresponsive)
- "Can't even move mouse" frustration

That margin makes the system feel cooperative instead of hostile.

